{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03020",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.39,
      "end_seconds": 7.5,
      "duration_seconds": 6.11,
      "text": "Hello, good to see you. Please sit. So, what's the main thing today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 8.77,
      "end_seconds": 13.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "Well, I've been having a severe headache for days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.9,
      "end_seconds": 17.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "How many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 19.29,
      "end_seconds": 22.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "I've had it for two months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.63,
      "end_seconds": 32.18,
      "duration_seconds": 9.55,
      "text": "Mm, okay. Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.48,
      "end_seconds": 45.65,
      "duration_seconds": 12.17,
      "text": "Okay, so a three out of ten, I suppose. Yes, lying down. That makes it worse. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.63,
      "end_seconds": 52.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.26,
      "end_seconds": 62.51,
      "duration_seconds": 9.25,
      "text": "Being sick goes along with it, most of the time. The being sick? That's been for one week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.23,
      "end_seconds": 66.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "How much does it limit you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.47,
      "end_seconds": 69.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "It feels severe to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.8,
      "end_seconds": 74.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.13,
      "end_seconds": 77.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "No, no conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.82,
      "end_seconds": 92.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.69,
      "end_seconds": 96.22,
      "duration_seconds": 1.53,
      "text": "No known allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.1,
      "end_seconds": 100.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Do you live by yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.05,
      "end_seconds": 104.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.24,
      "end_seconds": 113.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "So, do you get out much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.02,
      "end_seconds": 118.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.21,
      "end_seconds": 122.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.41,
      "end_seconds": 127.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.19,
      "text": "No, never."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.44,
      "end_seconds": 142.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "So, which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.65,
      "end_seconds": 150.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "I mean, I'm on the contraceptive pill, daily."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.21,
      "end_seconds": 165.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "A few quick ones: fever or weakness on one side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.0,
      "end_seconds": 170.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.26,
      "end_seconds": 175.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "And head injury, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.81,
      "end_seconds": 180.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.51,
      "text": "Um, no, I haven't had any head injury."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.92,
      "end_seconds": 184.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "I follow. Any breathing difficulties apart from this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.95,
      "end_seconds": 187.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "No, uh, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.93,
      "end_seconds": 191.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "I'll note down your vital signs first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.01,
      "end_seconds": 206.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.1,
      "end_seconds": 226.11,
      "duration_seconds": 8.01,
      "text": "Okay: heart rate 74, pressure 160 over 91, oxygen saturation is 99 percent, temperature 36.4."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.79,
      "end_seconds": 231.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "Let's move on to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 232.73,
      "end_seconds": 233.71,
      "duration_seconds": 0.98,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.54,
      "end_seconds": 236.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "Hold that for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.54,
      "end_seconds": 248.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "The optic discs look swollen and you are drowsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.2,
      "end_seconds": 255.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "You can sit up now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.14,
      "end_seconds": 277.72,
      "duration_seconds": 5.58,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression is this: It points towards possible cerebral venous thrombosis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 279.38,
      "end_seconds": 282.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Do you think it's something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.58,
      "end_seconds": 311.75,
      "duration_seconds": 28.17,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with possible cerebral venous thrombosis do well once it's treated properly. I think an urgent CT venogram makes sense here, for possible venous thrombosis. I'll request an MRI of the head, it'll help with papilloedema. Stop the pill, you need an urgent scan and admission. I'd like you to see the neurology team as well, and I'll write the referral."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 312.57,
      "end_seconds": 313.27,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.41,
      "end_seconds": 327.06,
      "duration_seconds": 12.65,
      "text": "The thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse. If that happens, go to emergency. Please come and see me straight away. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 328.32,
      "end_seconds": 332.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Well, great, thank you for your help."
    }
  ]
}